  "note": "The even side of Lenton Avenue in 1891, from the enumerator's page A. Hagues sent (image L16848_0). Six households at 4 to 14, which the record holds as #367 to #372 and for which it held no 1891 at all — it had 1901, 1911 and 1921 only. Five of the six heads are coachmen, which is what this side of the street was: the mews and stabling for the big houses, with the men who drove for them living over the yards.\n\nOnly two people here are bound to existing records. Arthur Sims (#2497) and Sarah (#2498) at 4 Lenton Avenue are already in the record from 1901 and 1911, and his birthplace of Duffield and his age agree with the page, so this adds 1891 to people who are already there. Their children on this page are NOT the children the record holds: Frederick 15, Gertrude 14 and John Henry 9 in 1891 were born about 1876, 1877 and 1882, while the record's Gertie (b.1890) and Arthur (b.1892) were born after this census. They are an older set of children and are entered as new people.\n\nNobody else here is in the record under any year — Beecroft Brown, Reuben Thompson, William Bell, Joseph Drake and William Hyde are all new. Reuben Thompson at 10 is not connected to the Henry Thompson family the record holds at 8 Lenton Avenue in 1901: different house, different forenames, different birthplaces.\n\nAges are as the enumerator wrote them, so a birth year worked back from one may be a year out either way. Where the page gives no age, none is invented.",
